A '''Fisher''' (Japanese: '''つりびと''' ''Fisher'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that first debuted in the [[Generation I]] games. Prior to [[Generation VIII]], they were known as '''Fisherman''', except in [[Pokémon Stadium]] and {{game2|Gold|Silver|Crystal}}, which also used "Fisher" due to text space concerns. They are typically depicted as middle-aged men with rods, reels, and fishing gear, with a {{i|Poké Ball}} used as a lure. However, younger Fishermen have been seen in {{g|X and Y}}, and in {{g|Sword and Shield}}, female Fishers were introduced.

In the Japanese version of {{game2|Gold|Silver|Crystal}}, they are depicted smoking, as fishermen smoking is a common stereotype in Japan. The cigarette was removed in international releases.

They specialize in {{type|Water}} Pokémon that can be caught via [[fishing]]. In most core series games, there is a Fisherman who will fight the player with a full team made up entirely of {{p|Magikarp}}. In the {{gal|Battle Tower}} in [[Galar]], Fishers use both {{type|Water}} Pokémon and those that may benefit from [[rain]].

In [[Generation VII]], they keep their Pokémon in [[Lure Ball]]s, while in Generation VIII, they keep them in [[Dive Ball]]s instead.

In [[Pokémon: Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!|Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!]], Fishermen will award three {{i|Poké Ball}}s along with [[prize money]] upon being defeated.

